course: dictionary
lesson: 5261
title: Names and capital letters
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A name is the special word we use for a person, a pet or a place. Jonathan is a name, so it begins with a capital letter, even when it is in the middle of a sentence.
explain: «Jonathan, King Saul's son, became David's best friend.» Here Jonathan is a person in a Bible story. «Jonathan, a giant tortoise on St Helena, is thought to have hatched around 1832.» Here the same name belongs to a tortoise. The spelling is the same, but the words around it tell you who or what is meant.
explain: Look for clues when you meet a name. Words like «tortoise», «island» or «King Saul's son» tell you who Jonathan is. Jon and Jonny are short forms of Jonathan, so if you see one of those, you can check the sentence for more clues.
fact: Jonathan is a common boy's first name.
fact: In the Bible, Jonathan was the son of King Saul and the loyal best friend of David.
fact: Jon and Jonny are short forms of Jonathan.
fact: Names always start with a capital letter, even in the middle of a sentence.
fact: «Jonathan», a giant tortoise on St Helena, is thought to have hatched around 1832 and is the oldest known living land animal.
exercise: Find the name in «Jonathan, a giant tortoise on St Helena, is thought to have hatched around 1832.» | hatched | *Jonathan | giant | tortoise
exercise: Why does «Jonathan» begin with a capital letter in «David's best friend was Jonathan»? | Because it is a verb | Because it is an important job | *Because it is a name | Because it is the longest word in the sentence
exercise: Jon and Jonny are short forms of which name? | Jonah | Joseph | *Jonathan | Jonas
test: «Jonathan, a giant tortoise on St Helena, is the oldest known living land animal.» What is Jonathan in this sentence? | A king from long ago | A boy in a school | A town on an island | *A giant tortoise
test: In the Bible story, whose best friend was Jonathan? | St Helena | King Saul | Samuel | *David
exam: Which sentence uses Jonathan as the name of a tortoise? | *«Jonathan, a giant tortoise on St Helena, is thought to have hatched around 1832.» | «Jonathan helped David escape from Saul.» | «Jonathan is a common boy's first name.» | «Jonathan, King Saul's son, became David's best friend.»
